    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i finally did it. i got the promotion and the vp title i've been working 80 hour weeks for since i was twenty. it's everything i said i wanted. but i'm sitting here in my office looking at the view and i just... i feel nothing. it's like i reached the top of the mountain and there's just nothing there. it's actually kind of terrifying. what was the point of all that climbing if this is all that's waiting at the top?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you've hit a wall, a very common feeling when the big goal is finally achieved. This emptiness, this \"nothingness,\" is often a sign that the chase was the real reward, not the destination itself. Perhaps it's time to look at what you *actually* want, beyond the titles and the view. Consider what would make the next climb feel worthwhile, even if it's a much smaller one.",
      "source": "target",
